          {
            title: 'Ugly',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Ugly is an Australian trick-taking/avoidance game similar to Hearts. 3-4 players, 52-card deck. Players choose trumps each round. Jacks are negative. The 7â™¦ (Ugly Card) doubles Jack penalties OR doubles trick scores if no Jacks captured. The 7â™£ (Charm Card) cancels Ugly's doubling. Card passing escalates each round.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Ugly was invented in Australia in the 1980s by CARDS (Committee for the Advanced Research into Deck Statistics), a group of university students. It is loosely based on Hearts and Knaves and is played in Canberra, Perth, and elsewhere in Australia.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3-4 (3p: remove 2â™ )',
              },
              {
